TableBlockContent.description:
Content for table blocks.

Table blocks support up to two levels of nesting in a single request.
When creating a table via the Append block children endpoint, the table
MUST include a 'children' array with at least 1 table_row block.
The table_width can only be set when the table is first created.

Note: The 'children' field is required when creating a table but is NOT
returned in API responses. To retrieve table rows, use the Retrieve block
children endpoint with the table block's ID.

Example structure for creating a table:
    {
        "type": "table",
        "object": "block",
        "table": {
            "table_width": 2,
            "has_column_header": true,
            "has_row_header": false,
            "children": [
                {
                    "type": "table_row",
                    "object": "block",
                    "table_row": {
                        "cells": [
                            [{"type": "text", "text": {"content": "Header 1"}}],
                            [{"type": "text", "text": {"content": "Header 2"}}]
                        ]
                    }
                }
            ]
        }
    }
